          "text": "ation, dead tuples\n-- and WAL churn on every cleanup delete, plus FOR KEY SHARE row locks on every consume\n-- INSERT contending with the cleanup DELETE's row locks. Nothing reads those columns back\n-- (write-only: INSERT + entity projection; the API DTO drops them) and snowflake ids are\n-- never reused, so dangling historical ids are harmless "
        }
